{
  "__comment__": "Hardware-free confocal with TWO single-photon detectors on ONE SIMULATED Swabian Time Tagger, counting photons per pixel: no laser sync, no STED, no FLIM. The timeTagger block declares its inputs by name (apd_green and apd_red on inputs 1 and 2, falling edge; the scan's line and frame clocks on 3 and 4); each detector (TT_green, TT_red) names its photon_input and has measurement 'counting', so every scan gives two images, one per input, from one card and one set of pixel markers. The mock card gives each input its own sample (red: the green sample with a brightness ramp across x), so the two images differ. The NI APD still runs alongside. The Lifetime widget's Signals panel finds each input's trigger level.",
